subtasks.details:
1. Define JSON Schema sanity_result.schema.json under GUI/schemas/:
   {
     "type": "object",
     "properties": {
       "summary": {"type": "object", "properties": {"info": {"type": "integer"}, "warning": {"type": "integer"}, "critical": {"type": "integer"}}},
       "messages": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {"level": {"enum": ["info", "warning", "critical"]}, "text": {"type": "string"}}}}
     }, "required": ["summary", "messages"]
   }
2. Implement `run_sanity_checks()` that executes `pw.x -check` (or provided command) with subprocess.check_output, decodes UTF-8, splits lines.
3. Use regex `r"\[(info|warning|critical)]\s*(.*)"` to classify lines; accumulate counts.
4. Return dict conforming to schema; validate with `jsonschema` package (add to dependencies).
5. Create Flask POST /check that calls the function and returns 200 with JSON or 500 on subprocess error.
6. Provide CLI fallback `python -m qe_gui_server --check` for manual testing.
